<title>FRANCE: Credit du Nord makes 1996 net attrib profit.</title>
<headline>Credit du Nord makes 1996 net attrib profit.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable		 profit  191.1  vs   loss   14.3</p>
<p>    Net					    213.6  vs	     4.6</p>
<p>    Net interest and various	     3,304.2  vs	 3,272.7</p>
<p>    Commissions				2,147.0  vs	 1,974.4</p>
<p>    Global operating production	  5,500.4  vs	 5,284.3</p>
<p>    Operating charges			4,541.6  vs	 4,569.5</p>
<p>    Gross operating			    836.8  vs	   714.8</p>
<p>    Provisions		  charge	 529.6  vs charge  704.1</p>
<p>    Company tax				  46.9   vs	    40.5</p>
<p>    Extraordinary result	 loss	46.7   vs	    34.4</p>
<p>NOTE - Credit du Nord is being sold by Paribas to Societe Generale for 2.2 billion francs under a deal which Paribas said on Tuesday had now been signed.</p>
<p>Credit du Nord said in its results statement 1996 marked its return to profitability and that risk provisioning reached 63.1 percent at the end of 1996 from 59.1 percent at end-1995.</p>
<p>It said it had included 50 million francs in extraordinary charges to cover preparations for the euro single currency in the European Union and 41.6 million for change of Paris offices.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
